scripts/.rho_g7e_*


# Compiled producer binaries under coordination/. Excluded from snapshot
# archives on purpose: they are rebuildable from the declared source (cnt.c,
# sq_null.c, probe.c, all archived), they are not reproducible across machines,
# and an archive that declares them would fail verification whenever a rebuild
# changed a byte. The SOURCE is the artifact; the binary is not.
coordination/goals/*/batches/*/tasks/*/cnt
coordination/goals/*/batches/*/tasks/*/sq_null
coordination/goals/*/batches/*/tasks/*/probe
coordination/goals/*/batches/*/tasks/*/mini
coordination/goals/*/batches/*/tasks/*/mini2
coordination/goals/*/batches/*/tasks/*/count5
coordination/goals/*/batches/*/tasks/*/pin

# In-flight producer working directory for GOAL-ECDLP-001 BATCH-028.
# REMOVED BY THE SNAPSHOT ARCHIVE TASK-20260802-d34ac4, IN A COMMIT THAT PRECEDES IT.
# Rationale, learned the hard way in GOAL-AES-003 and recorded as CORR-20260802-009:
# a dispatcher-verified archive must INTRODUCE every path it declares. Producer
# artifacts swept into an earlier commit by `git add -A` can never afterwards be
# bound by the archive that is supposed to bind them, and BATCH-001's ledger archive
# is permanently "published but not official" for exactly that reason.

# The frozen EXP-SMTH-4403c4 contract is a DECLARED ARTIFACT of TASK-20260802-80f5e9
# and must be INTRODUCED by the snapshot archive TASK-20260802-d34ac4, same rule as the
# producer tree above. Its freeze is enforced by sha256 in freeze_receipt.json and
# re-checked by the executing task, not by being committed early.

# The two BATCH-028 reviewer directories, until the ledger archive TASK-20260802-268ec9
# introduces them. NARROW BY DESIGN: the producer tree above is already committed by the
# snapshot archive, so only these two paths are held back.
# Committing a reviewer report early is the exact defect that left GOAL-AES-003 BATCH-001's
# ledger archive permanently "published but not official" (CORR-20260802-009): an archive can
# only bind content it INTRODUCES, and a report swept in by an earlier commit can never
# afterwards be bound by the archive meant to bind it.

# BATCH-029 in-flight producer tree, until the snapshot archive TASK-20260802-8c84fe
# introduces it. Same rule as BATCH-028: a dispatcher-verified archive can only bind
# content it INTRODUCES, so an artifact swept into an earlier commit can never afterwards
# be bound by the archive meant to bind it. The archive removes this entry when it stages.
# experiments/EXP-SMTH-e932e8/ is deliberately NOT listed here yet -- the contract does not
# exist until the freeze task writes it, and it gets the same treatment then.
coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-003/tasks/TASK-20260802-4500d4/collide
coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-003/tasks/TASK-20260802-447db8/sq_slot

# The two AES BATCH-003 reviewer directories, until the ledger archive
# TASK-20260802-4072e6 introduces them. Committing a reviewer report early is the
# exact defect that left GOAL-AES-003 BATCH-001's ledger archive permanently
# published-but-not-official (CORR-20260802-009), and that I repeated an hour ago
# with ECDLP BATCH-029's approval record. An archive can only bind content it
# INTRODUCES.

# experiments/EXP-SMTH-4403c4/ ignore REMOVED: PR #144 landed the frozen
# contract + measurement package; run manifests must be trackable for
# validate_ledger (EV-DS-84d006 cites RUN-SMTH-4403c4-*).

# AutoLab executor staging area (orchestration/executors/autolab.py). Anchored
# at the repository root, so experiments/<EXP>/runs/ — the immutable run
# records validate_ledger and check_run_immutability enforce — stay tracked.
# These are pre-ledger execution outputs, not run records: an AutoLab result
# enters the ledger by being converted into a RUN-* record under experiments/,
# never by being swept in from here. CORR-20260802-009 is the standing lesson:
# an artifact caught by an earlier `git add -A` can never afterwards be bound
# by the archive that is supposed to bind it.
/runs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED ARTIFACTS — never committed.
#
# Each of these is derived, byte-for-byte, from files that ARE committed. While
# they were tracked they sat in the top five conflict paths of the repository:
# every branch that added a knowledge entry rewrote the whole of INDEX.md, and
# every branch that touched a queue rewrote its whole plan. Two agents doing
# unrelated work therefore conflicted on files that carry no information of
# their own.
#
# Rebuild locally with:
#   python3 tools/build_knowledge_index.py
#   python3 tools/research_dispatch.py <queue> --output <dir>/dispatch_plan.json \
#                                              --report <dir>/dispatch_plan.md
# CI regenerates both and fails if the corpus or a queue does not build.
#
# MIGRATION NOTE for open branches: main DELETES these paths, so a branch that
# still modifies them will hit a delete/modify conflict on its next merge. That
# is a one-time mechanical conflict whose only correct resolution is `git rm`,
# and tools/sync_open_branches.py resolves it automatically for exactly these
# paths. It is deliberately preferred over the recurring content conflict it
# replaces.
knowledge/INDEX.md
# Rendered from knowledge/frontiers/ecdlp/<area>/KR-*.yaml by
# tools/build_frontier_map.py; derived exactly like INDEX.md.
knowledge/frontiers/ecdlp/MAP.md
# tools/lead_atlas.py --render; derived from knowledge/leads/ecdlp/<family>/.
knowledge/leads/ecdlp/ATLAS.md
# Compact per-record indexes of ledger/proposals, ledger/hypotheses and
# experiments/*/specification.yaml, built by tools/build_ledger_index.py so a
# dedup or orientation step greps ~6 MB instead of reading an 80 MB corpus.
# Derived exactly like INDEX.md; CI rebuilds it (--check-builds).
ledger/.index/

# The static dashboard, rendered from ledger/, experiments/ and knowledge/ by
# `python3 -m ui.build` (`make ui-build`). ~125 MB across ~14,700 files, all of
# it derived: committing it would add the whole corpus to the repository a
# second time, in a form that changes on every merge. GitHub Pages publishes it
# from .github/workflows/pages.yml, which builds it fresh on each push to main.
/site/
/site-report.json
# BY NAME, AT ANY DEPTH. This was five hand-maintained globs -- one per
# directory shape someone had found so far: batches/, batches/*/plan/,
# batches/*/*/ for the one-queue-per-work-unit goals, then reconciliation/
# after "a RECON campaign's plan was landing untracked". Each was correct and
# each was discovered the same way, by a generated file reaching main through
# a shape no existing glob covered. 26 of them were tracked when this was
# written, under proposals/, under ideation/, and inside a replication
# directory holding a nested copy of the coordination tree -- none reachable
# by any of the five.
#
# A dispatch plan is generated wherever it sits, so the rule is the FILENAME,
# not the location. This still names the exact artifact rather than a
# directory: a directory ignore silently swallows artifacts that do not exist
# yet (CORR-20260803-ba2eb7), and a RECON campaign's audit output must stay
# visible so its Coordinator archive can INTRODUCE it (CORR-20260802-009).
**/dispatch_plan.json
**/dispatch_plan.md

coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-004/tasks/TASK-20260803-6ba122/nib
coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-004/tasks/TASK-20260803-6ba122/mini_b1
coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-004/tasks/TASK-20260803-367b1b/sq_slot
coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-004/tasks/TASK-20260803-367b1b/yoyo_sbox
coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-004/tasks/TASK-20260803-367b1b/yoyo_sbox_v2

coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-005/tasks/TASK-20260803-48a239/rc7_aesni_vec
coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-005/tasks/TASK-20260803-48a239/yoyo_sbox_v2

coordination/goals/GOAL-AES-003/batches/BATCH-006/tasks/TASK-20260803-0764fc/yoyo_sbox_v2
