# Local OpenCode runtime lock/session state (pid, hostname, claim tokens).
# Ephemeral per-machine process-coordination state, not a research artifact;
# a `git add -A` in a dispatch worktree swept it into a commit once and it
# nearly reached main. See CORR-20260809 merge-contamination note.
.opencode/goals/state.json.lock
.opencode/goals/state.json.sessions/

# Sibling git worktrees accidentally captured as gitlinks by the same
# `git add -A`. These point at commits local to other worktrees on this
# machine and are meaningless (and potentially dangling) anywhere else.
.worktrees/
/.tmp/

# cairn (docs/cairn-integration-plan.md): the checkers and objectives under
# cairn/ are committed source, pinned by hash -- but the LOG is state, not a
# generated artifact, and it belongs outside the tree entirely (plan section
# 5). tools/cairn_bridge.py defaults it to ~/.cairn/, so these only fire for
# someone who pointed CAIRN_LOG inside the checkout anyway; the rule stays
# defense in depth against exactly the concurrent-worktree hazard the plan
# describes -- two worktrees committing "their" copy of one writer's log.
cairn.jsonl
cairn.pending.json
*.objective-ids.json
# Separate from the above: distributed-researcher's blob store is keyed off
# --root, not --log (src/blobs.rs STORE_DIR = ".cairn/blobs"), and this
# bridge points --root at this checkout so checkers resolve by their
# committed repo-relative path. That makes a `.cairn/` directory here a
# side effect of running the CLI at all, not something anyone chose to put
# in the tree -- found by it happening once during this integration's own
# testing.
/.cairn/

# Formal lane scratch (docs/mathcode-integration.md). The MathCode engine is an
# autonomous coding agent, so each attempt runs in its own throwaway directory
# OUTSIDE the Lean workspace -- LeanWorker scans every .lean file under
# formal/, and one abandoned candidate carrying `sorry` would mark every later
# task in that workspace INVALID. Attempts are kept on disk (a failed
# formalization is the record of what was tried) but never committed: the
# committed artifact is the staged theorem plus the proof artifact's hashes.
.formal-attempts/
# The engine's own output directory, if anyone runs `mathcode` by hand at the
# repository root rather than through `autoresearch formal`.
LeanFormalizations/

# Lean build products and the generated root module of the formal workspace.
# formal/CryptoResearch.lean lists the staged theorem modules so lake builds
# them; it is derived from the directory (tools/rebuild_formal_root.py) and
# regenerated by the formalize pipeline before every verification, so
# committing it would be one more shared file for concurrent worktrees to
# conflict over. lean-toolchain and lake-manifest.json ARE committed -- those
# two are the pin a later verification reproduces against.
formal/.lake/
formal/CryptoResearch.lean

# EXP-ECDLP-e36df2's driver appends to this for the whole duration of its
# Stage 2/3 run (a multi-hour single-process job) -- committing it would mean
# a new commit every time the stop hook notices it grew. Not a required
# deliverable of TASK-20260911-9df234 (the run/manifest/raw-result and
# pooled-summary artifacts carry the scientific content); kept on disk for
# operational visibility only. Path-scoped, not by filename, since
# "full_run.log" is this one driver's own shell-redirect choice, not a
# standardized artifact name other experiments share.
experiments/EXP-ECDLP-e36df2/driver/full_run.log

# Compiled WDSat binaries inside ICPERF run packages. EXP-ICPERF-66fd51
# rebuilds WDSat per instance because that solver sizes its allocation at
# COMPILE time, so one run package contains 20-32 near-identical binaries of a
# few hundred KiB each. They are reproducible from what is committed: the
# sources beside them, environment.json's wdsat_src_sha256, and each row's
# wdsat_constants recording the sizing it was built for. RUN-ICPERF-4ec9b9's
# manifest declares the exclusion in artifacts.builds_excluded_from_archive.
# Path-scoped to the binary name, so the build's sources, make.log and
# config_used.json stay committed -- those are what a reviewer rebuilds from,
# and the V2 joint of REVIEW-ICPERF-20260913-66fd51 did exactly that.
experiments/*/runs/*/builds/*/wdsat_solver
analysis/qsp-ecc2k130/explore/gf2rc
analysis/qsp-ecc2k130/explore/explore.log
analysis/qsp-ecc2k130/explore/explore_fast.log
analysis/qsp-ecc2k130/explore/__pycache__/
analysis/qsp-ecc2k130/explore/shape_census_131.log
experiments/EXP-QSP-33b442/implementation/gf2rc

